       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5 to 10 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You're not a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who has assessed the patient. I can't verify that this order was intended or authorized.\n\nPlease ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose. If they confirm a standard dose such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, I can enter it right away. If the prescriber really does intend 50 mg, they should enter and document it themselves, and pharmacy will probably need to review it."
      }
